{"name":"Bindi Red","hex":"#b0003c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bindi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The “holy dot” traditionally worn on the forehead of Hindu women.","Makeup or jewellery worn in imitation of such a dot."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The common lawn weed, Soliva sessilis, introduced to Australia from South America.","A seed of this plant, having small sharp spines which stick painfully into bare feet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bindi"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bindi","blocks":[{"text":"A bindi is a coloured dot or, in modern times, a sticker worn on the centre of the forehead, by Hindus, Jains, and Buddhists from the Indian subcontinent. While there are regional variations, traditional bindis are red or maroon, made with material such as kumkum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Kullu_Himachal_Pradesh_India_Woman.jpg/330px-Kullu_Himachal_Pradesh_India_Woman.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bindi"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Indian_Dancer_%28Malabika_Sen%29.jpg/500px-Indian_Dancer_%28Malabika_Sen%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Indian_Dancer_%28Malabika_Sen%29.jpg/500px-Indian_Dancer_%28Malabika_Sen%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIndianDancer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Female_figure_with_hair_ornaments%2C_terracotta%2C_200-250_BCE.jpg/500px-Female_figure_with_hair_ornaments%2C_terracotta%2C_200-250_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Female_figure_with_hair_ornaments%2C_terracotta%2C_200-250_BCE.jpg/500px-Female_figure_with_hair_ornaments%2C_terracotta%2C_200-250_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Female figure with bindi ornament, terracotta, 200–250 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFemale_figure_with_hair_ornaments%2C_terracotta%2C_200-250_BCE.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Prajnaparamita_Java.jpg/500px-Prajnaparamita_Java.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Prajnaparamita_Java.jpg/500px-Prajnaparamita_Java